The <meta> tag provides information about the HTML document, not the content itself.
- meta = information about the webpage

Examples of meta tags:
a. meta charset="UTF-8"
utf-8: It encode or transform the characters to (binary) bytes and bytes to characters which make computer to understand the text.
charset: collection of characters. 
   - It specifies the character encoding for the HTML document.

b. meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"
viewport: the visible area of a webpage on different devices. (responsive design)
<meta name="keywords" content="HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Web Development, Programming">
//they used to show in website search results when we search for related topics.

<!-- Video -->
<video controls width="300">
  <source src="video.mp4" type="video/mp4">
</video>

<!-- Audio -->
<audio controls>
  <source src="audio.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
</audio>

<!-- Iframe -->: It is used to embed another HTML page within the current page and also we can add other resources like videos, maps etc.
<iframe src="https://example.com" width="300" height="200"></iframe>

